{
  "id": "grammar.a2.14.01.directas",
  "title": "Direct Questions About Past Events",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Direct questions ask for information about a completed event. Use an interrogative word with the pretérito indefinido: ¿*Qué* *pasó*? ¿*Dónde* *trabajaste*? ¿*Cuándo* *llegaste*? ¿*Cómo* *empezó* la *entrevista*? The question word comes first."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "¿Qué pasó?",
          "english": "What happened?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Dónde trabajaste?",
          "english": "Where did you work?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Cuándo llegaste?",
          "english": "When did you arrive?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Cómo empezó la entrevista?",
          "english": "How did the interview start?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "qué",
          "what"
        ],
        [
          "dónde",
          "where"
        ],
        [
          "cuándo",
          "when"
        ],
        [
          "cómo",
          "how"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Every question word here carries a written accent — *qué*, *dónde*, *cuándo*, *cómo* — precisely because it's asking rather than relating. Drop the accent and *dónde* turns into the relative 'where' instead of a question word."
    },
    {
      "type": "external-link",
      "topic": "indirect questions",
      "site": "Lingolia",
      "url": "https://www.lingolia.com/en/grammar/sentence-structure/indirect-questions"
    }
  ]
}
